  "tidy.preset.trim": "Trim teeth",
  "tidy.preset.line": "Smooth borders",
  "tidy.preset.line.hint": "Redraws borders as gentle lines (the vector-line way).\n· Straighten borders, 16 edges: a gentle line through the middle of the stairs and zigzags; faces near it take the colour of the side their centre is on. Stairs and bends shorter than 16 border edges straighten.\n· Then 3 passes of trimming teeth for spikes still sticking out.\n· Longer curves (the shape of a part) stay — a thin line keeps both its borders. Protected colours stay.\n· Steps smaller than a triangle stay. The mixing settings are left as they are.",
  "tidy.preset.crisp.hint": "Straightens the borders between colours.\n· 6 smoothing passes: ragged faces along a border take the colour most of their neighbours have.\n· Specks under 300 faces go to the colour around them, so borders lose their crumbs.\n· Mixing: up to 2 filaments in thirds, the shortest layer repeat, so mixed edges show the fewest stripes.\n→ For clean, cartoon-like colour areas. Tiny dots (eye highlights) can vanish, so protect them first.",
  "tidy.preset.gradient.hint": "Keeps shading (light to dark) as many small steps.\n· At least 32 colours: similar shades are merged less, so a shading stays a fine staircase (with few colours it clumps into 2–3 steps).\n· 1 smoothing pass, islands under 40 faces only: the steps are hardly touched.\n· Mixing: up to 3 filaments at 25 %, so in-between colours are finer and steps smaller.\n→ The result is a fine staircase, not a smooth flow. More colours make slicing heavier, and mixed colours can show layer stripes.",
  "tidy.preset.solid.hint": "Paints each part one flat colour.\n· 1–2 groups per colour family (6–16 in all): the light and shadow of one part become one colour.\n· 8 smoothing passes, islands under 600 faces absorbed: clean areas, no blotches.\n· Mixing: thirds, and a colour within ΔE 10 of a loaded filament prints as that filament, not a mix — fewer stripes.\n→ For toy-like models with clear colour areas. Shading such as shadows and blush goes.",
  "tidy.preset.detail.hint": "Keeps small colour bits.\n· Anything over 20 faces stays: small dots and patterns survive.\n· Only 2 smoothing passes: thin lines wear less.\n· Small vivid colours (pupils, cheeks, ribbon accents) are protected automatically.\n· Mixing: accent colours are mapped on their own, not lost among similar ones.\n→ In return, more ragged edges and blotches stay too.",
  "tidy.preset.trim.hint": "Trims thin triangles sticking out of borders (spikes).\n· A triangle with two sides or more against other colours goes to the colour it borders longer. 3 passes = spikes up to three deep.\n· A furry-looking border becomes a clean staircase; steps smaller than a triangle stay.\n· A line one face wide keeps its middle and wears a little at the ends. Protected colours stay.\n· The mixing settings are left as they are.",
